# Hygiene (MC30): x:t_wice< binds a local t around the text of its
# call; the macro phase renames that binder to a fresh name, so the
# program's own t (5) is the one its text sees: 2 * (5 + 1).
== SOURCE
"x:" u_se< "Macros"
t := 5
@ x:t_wice< "t + 1"
== EXPAND
"x:" u_se< "Macros"
t := 5
{ @ -> g1:t := 2; g1:t * (t + 1) } @
== RESULT
12
